The test vehicle travels at target speed V1 on a straight road. A cyclist waiting to cross the current lane is positioned on the left/right side of the current lane, with a distance D between the cyclist and the lane centerline. When the longitudinal separation distance between the test vehicle and the cyclist is d, the cyclist crosses the current lane from the left/right side of the test vehicle at speed V2. The time required for the test vehicle to reach the collision point is identical to the time required for the cyclist to reach the collision point.